ANSYS structural sim = `65_final_0723/pymapdl_simulation_ver5_fibrous.py` (PyMAPDL). Run: `PATH=/home/jeff/miniconda3/envs/ansys_new/bin:$PATH python pymapdl_simulation_ver5_fibrous.py <start> <end> <nproc>` (end exclusive).

Per case: `.msh → .cdb` (meshio+pyvista, reads gmsh:physical tags) → launch MAPDL (`/opt/cvbml/softwares/ansys_inc/v251/ansys/bin/ansys251`) → solve peak & low → FC results `.vtk`. Two_sides(tag 6) fixed; wall pressure mapped via `/MAP` onto WALL_IN_VESSEL(4)+WALL_IN_FC(5).

**Inputs (all staged on cvbml02 2026-07-23):**
- mesh: script edited so `msh_path = case_dir/type2_mesh/solid_type_2_quad_curved.msh` (user fixed on curved Type2; original `.bak_type1` reads solid_type_1.msh). See [[solid-mesh-two-types]].
- `pre_data/material.json` (vessel mat1/lipid mat2/fc mat3/cal mat8; ρ,ν only) + E per case from `pre_data/parameter.csv` (E_vessel/E_lipid/E_fc/E_cal).
- `post_data/wall_0723/{peak,low}/wall_{bc}_case_<i>.csv` — wall pressure BC (cols x,y,z,Tx,Ty,Tz,Pressure; /MAP reads col7). Generated by the fluid/lumen side on cvbml01; copied to cvbml02 (lumen NOT run on cvbml02, see [[focus-solid-not-lumen]]).

**Env ready on cvbml02:** ANSYS MAPDL exec present; pymapdl 0.70.2, ansys.mapdl.reader, utils.utils_ansys.utils_prep/utils_bc all import (utils via master_python editable). See [[solid-mesh-env-cv1]].

Scale caveat: curved Type2 is ~3.6M quadratic tets / 5.25M nodes → msh→cdb + solve is memory/time heavy.
